This product includes software developed by OpenAI:
OpenAI Codex
https://github.com/openai/codex, commit ac54a05
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see third_party/codex/LICENSE
and third_party/codex/NOTICE).

third_party/codex holds Codex's own files, unmodified: LICENSE, NOTICE, its
goal extension (codex-rs/ext/goal: source, prompt templates and tests), and
the two files that extension's prompts depend on
(codex-rs/prompts/src/update_plan_instructions.rs and
codex-rs/core/src/context/user_goal.rs). The rest of Codex is left out.
Guardian's goal loop sends Codex's continuation and objective-updated prompts
word for word, and its get_goal and update_goal tools carry Codex's names,
descriptions and statuses. Codex's Rust runtime is not run: it is built into
Codex's own agent. scripts/gen-vendored.mjs reads the text out of these files
into packages/core/src/goal/vendored.generated.ts.

This product includes software developed by DeepSeek:
DeepSeek Harness
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, commit fcc0ad4
Licensed under the MIT License (see third_party/deepseek-harness/LICENSE).

third_party/deepseek-harness holds DeepSeek Harness's own files, unmodified:
LICENSE, its goal packages (packages/goal: goal, goal-round-driver, tool-goal
and command-goal, with their tests and documentation) and
docs/subsystems/goal.md. The rest of the harness is left out. Guardian runs
two of its functions as they are, with types stripped: renderGoalRoundPrompt
(the <goal_round> prompt) and renderWrapupContext (the closing instructions),
and uses its blocked-round threshold and refusal message. Its goal service,
round driver and tool plumbing are not run: they are built on the harness's
own framework.

This product includes software developed by Scale AI:
Monitor Red Teaming (MRT), the code of "Reliable Weak-to-Strong Monitoring of
LLM Agents"
https://github.com/scaleapi/mrt, commit 3535620
Licensed under the MIT License (see third_party/mrt/LICENSE).

third_party/mrt holds MRT's own files, unmodified, at their upstream paths:
LICENSE, README.md, the monitor (utils/pipeline_utils.py), its prompts
(task_pairs/base_task_definition.py), its transcript format and verdict parser
(utils/logging_utils.py, utils/analysis_utils.py), llms/base.py, and the
modules those import. third_party/mrt/VENDORED.md, which is Guardian's, lists
them and what is left out (the benchmark, the API providers, the experiment
scripts and notebooks). Guardian runs MRT's hierarchical and sequential
monitors as they are, with MRT's prompts, on the bundled Python; its adapter is
packages/monitor. The hybrid score, 0.5 x hierarchical + 0.5 x sequential, is
one line of Guardian's, from the paper's section 3.5: MRT's repository has no
code for it.
